### Localhost Environment Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### -----------------------------------------------------------
### MOVIES ENDPOINTS
### -----------------------------------------------------------

### 1. Get all movies
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies HTTP/1.1

### 2. Get single movie by ID (replace with a real ID from your database)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e HTTP/1.1

### 3. Create a new movie
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Interstellar",
  "director": "Christopher Nolan",
  "releaseYear": 2014,
  "genre": "Sci-Fi",
  "rating": 8.7,
  "runtime": 169,
  "synopsis": "When Earth becomes uninhabitable in the future, a farmer and ex-NASA pilot is tasked with piloting a spacecraft to find a new planet for humans.",
  "language": "English",
  "posterUrl": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BZjdkOTU3MDktN2IxOS00OGEyLWFmMjktY2FiMmZkNWIyODZiXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyMTMxODk2OTU@._V1_.jpg"
}

### 4. Create another movie (for testing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spirited Away",
  "director": "Hayao Miyazaki",
  "releaseYear": 2001,
  "genre": "Animation",
  "rating": 8.6,
  "runtime": 125,
  "synopsis": "During her family's move to the suburbs, a sullen 10-year-old girl wanders into a world ruled by gods, witches, and spirits.",
  "language": "Japanese",
  "posterUrl": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjlmZmI5MDctNDE2YS00YWE5LWE5ZWItZDBhYWQ0NTcxNWRhXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyMTMxODk2OTU@._V1_.jpg"
}

### 5. Update a movie by ID (replace with an inserted movie ID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Interstellar (IMAX Edition)",
  "director": "Christopher Nolan",
  "releaseYear": 2014,
  "genre": "Sci-Fi / Adventure",
  "rating": 8.9,
  "runtime": 169,
  "synopsis": "When Earth becomes uninhabitable, a team of explorers undertakes the most important mission in human history across the cosmos.",
  "language": "English",
  "posterUrl": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BZjdkOTU3MDktN2IxOS00OGEyLWFmMjktY2FiMmZkNWIyODZiXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyMTMxODk2OTU@._V1_.jpg"
}

### 6. Delete a movie by ID (replace with an inserted movie ID)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e HTTP/1.1

### -----------------------------------------------------------
### REVIEWS ENDPOINTS
### -----------------------------------------------------------

### 7. Get all reviews
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews HTTP/1.1

### 8. Get single review by ID (replace with a real review ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d2f HTTP/1.1

### 9. Create a new review
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "movieId": "651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e",
  "reviewerName": "Sarah Connor",
  "rating": 10,
  "comment": "An extraordinary journey through space and time. Emotional and scientifically thoughtful.",
  "reviewDate": "2024-04-12"
}

### 10. Update a review by ID (replace with an inserted review ID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/reviews/651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d2f HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "movieId": "651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e",
  "reviewerName": "Sarah Connor",
  "rating": 9.5,
  "comment": "Updated thoughts: still phenomenal on rewatch!",
  "reviewDate": "2024-04-15"
}

### 11. Delete a review by ID (replace with an inserted review ID)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/reviews/651a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d2f HTTP/1.1
